text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'As Adaptive Automaton enters the battlefield, choose a creature type.\\nAdaptive Automaton is the chosen type in addition to its other types.\\nOther creatures you control of the chosen type get +1/+1.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a Goblin.\\nGoblin Grenade deals 5 damage to any target.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nFling deals damage equal to the sacrificed creature's power to any target.", 'As long as Thran Golem is enchanted, it gets +2/+2 and has flying, first strike, and trample.', 'As long as you control a Griffin creature, Griffin Rider gets +3/+3 and has flying.', "At the beginning of each player's draw step, that player draws an additional card.\\nEach player may play an additional land on each of their turns.", "At the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player sacrifices a non-Zombie creature.\\nAt the beginning of the end step, if no creatures are on the battlefield, sacrifice Call to the Grave.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a lore counter on Mind Unbound, then draw a card for each lore counter on Mind Unbound.', 'Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)', 'Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nFlying', "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nIslandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Bloodthirst 2 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.)', 'Bloodthirst 2 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nLifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', "Bloodthirst 2 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nMenace (This creature can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", 'Bloodthirst 3 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nFlying\\nWhenever you cast a Vampire creature spell, it gains bloodthirst 3.', "Bloodthirst 3 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nTrample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Bloodthirst 6 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with six +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nFlying', "Chandra's Outrage deals 4 damage to target creature and 2 damage to that creature's controller.", 'Choose target creature you control. Whenever that creature deals combat damage to a player or planeswalker this turn, draw that many cards.', 'Copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Counter target noncreature spell.', 'Counter target red or green spell.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', 'Counter target spell.', "Creatures you control gain intimidate until end of turn. (Each of those creatures can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", 'Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control have flying.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)\\nWhen Acidic Slime enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact, enchantment, or land.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)\\nWhenever combat damage is dealt to you or a planeswalker you control, if Vengeful Pharaoh is in your graveyard, destroy target attacking creature, then put Vengeful Pharaoh on top of your library.', 'Deathtouch\\nWhenever Grave Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhen Roc Egg dies, create a 3/3 white Bird creature token with flying.", 'Defender\\nWhenever Pride Guardian blocks, you gain 3 life.', 'Destroy all creatures.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target creature with flying.', 'Destroy target enchantment.', 'Destroy target green or white creature.', "Destroy target land. Creatures without flying can't block this turn.", 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', 'Discard two cards: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', 'Dragonskull Summit enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Swamp or a Mountain.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', 'Draw a card. If a graveyard has twenty or more cards in it, draw three cards instead.', 'Draw two cards.', 'Drowned Catacomb enters the battlefield tapped unless you control an Island or a Swamp.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', 'During your turn, prevent all damage that would be dealt to you.', "During your turn, your opponents can't cast spells or activate abilities of artifacts, creatures, or enchantments.", 'Each player loses 1 life, discards a card, sacrifices a creature, then sacrifices a land.', 'Each player shuffles their hand and graveyard into their library, then draws seven cards. Exile Time Reversal.', 'Enchant creature or land\\nWhen enchanted permanent becomes tapped, destroy it.', 'Enchant creature\\nAll creatures able to block enchanted creature do so.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.\\nAt the beginning of the end step, if enchanted creature's power is 4 or greater, destroy Arachnus Web.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.\\nWhen enchanted creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, destroy Ice Cage.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and has protection from creatures.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has "{1}{G}: Regenerate this creature." (The next time the creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn\'t. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has haste.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +4/+4, has flying and first strike, and is an Angel in addition to its other types.\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, return Angelic Destiny to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has flying.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has lifelink. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen Dark Favor enters the battlefield, you lose 1 life.\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen Divine Favor enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3.', 'Enchant creature\\nYou control enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Equipped creature gets +0/+3.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Equipped creature gets +3/+0.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Equipped creature has hexproof and haste. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nEquip {1}", 'Exile target black or red permanent.', 'Flying', 'Flying (This creature can\'t be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Aegis Angel enters the battlefield, another target permanent gains indestructible for as long as you control Aegis Angel. (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it. A creature with indestructible can\'t be destroyed by damage.)', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Vampire this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Vampire.", 'Flying, haste', 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nDjinn of Wishes enters the battlefield with three wish counters on it.\\n{2}{U}{U}, Remove a wish counter from Djinn of Wishes: Reveal the top card of your library. You may play that card without paying its mana cost. If you don't, exile it.", 'Flying\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', "Flying\\nHaste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nWhenever an opponent is dealt damage by a red instant or sorcery spell you control or by a red planeswalker you control, return Chandra's Phoenix from your graveyard to your hand.", "Flying\\nHexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'Flying\\nSacrifice a creature: Devouring Swarm gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nSkywinder Drake can block only creatures with flying.', "Flying\\nVigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Archon of Justice dies, exile target permanent.', 'Flying\\nWhen Phantasmal Dragon becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'Flying\\nWhen Rune-Scarred Demon enters the battlefield, search your library for a card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sphinx of Uthuun enters the battlefield, reveal the top five cards of your library. An opponent separates those cards into two piles. Put one pile into your hand and the other into your graveyard.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Chasm Drake attacks, target creature you control gains flying until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Flameblast Dragon attacks, you may pay {X}{R}. If you do, Flameblast Dragon deals X damage to any target.', "Flying\\nWhenever a source deals damage to Belltower Sphinx, that source's controller mills that many cards.", 'Flying\\n{B}: Drifting Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'For each creature you control, you may search your library for a creature card with the same name as that creature. Put those cards onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'For each nonland permanent, choose a player at random. Then each player gains control of each permanent for which they were chosen. Untap those permanents.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', 'Glacial Fortress enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Plains or an Island.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nOther Goblin creatures you control get +1/+1 and have haste.', "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nDungrove Elder's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Forests you control.", 'If you have less life than an opponent, you gain 6 life. If you control fewer creatures than an opponent, create three 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.', "Illusion creatures you control get +1/+1 and have hexproof. (They can't be the targets of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "Incinerate deals 3 damage to any target. A creature dealt damage this way can't be regenerated this turn.", "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nHarbor Serpent can't attack unless there are five or more Islands on the battlefield.", 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Lifelink', 'Look at the top three cards of your library, then put them back in any order. You may shuffle.\\nDraw a card.', 'Other Elf creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Add {G} for each Elf you control.', 'Other Zombie creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{2}{B}, {T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', 'Pentavus enters the battlefield with five +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Pentavus: Create a 1/1 colorless Pentavite artifact creature token with flying.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a Pentavite: Put a +1/+1 counter on Pentavus.', 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Primordial Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, double the number of +1/+1 counters on Primordial Hydra.\\nPrimordial Hydra has trample as long as it has ten or more +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Put target card from your graveyard on top of your library.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach\\nTap an untapped Spider you control: Search your graveyard and/or library for a card named Arachnus Web and put it onto the battlefield attached to target creature. If you search your library this way, shuffle.', 'Reach\\nWhen Stingerfling Spider enters the battlefield, you may destroy target creature with flying.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Rootbound Crag enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Mountain or a Forest.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Rusted Sentinel enters the battlefield tapped.', 'Sacrifice Brindle Boar: You gain 4 life.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', "Sorin's Thirst deals 2 damage to target creature and you gain 2 life.", "Sorin's Vengeance deals 10 damage to target player or planeswalker and you gain 10 life.", "Spells you control can't be countered by blue or black spells this turn, and creatures you control can't be the targets of blue or black spells this turn.", 'Spend only black mana on X.\\nConsume Spirit deals X damage to any target and you gain X life.', 'Sunpetal Grove enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Forest or a Plains.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', "Tap up to two target creatures. Those creatures don't untap during their controller's next untap step.", 'Target creature gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains flying until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'Target creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -3/-1 until end of turn.', 'Target player chooses a card in their hand and discards the rest.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player reveals their hand. You choose a nonland card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Taste of Blood deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker and you gain 1 life.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nCombust deals 5 damage to target white or blue creature. The damage can't be prevented.", 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', "Tormented Soul can't block and can't be blocked.", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nWhen Crumbling Colossus attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.", "Trample\\nAs Sutured Ghoul enters the battlefield, exile any number of creature cards from your graveyard.\\nSutured Ghoul's power is equal to the total power of the exiled cards and its toughness is equal to their total toughness.", "Trample\\nPlay with the top card of your library revealed.\\nYou may cast creature spells from the top of your library. (Do this only any time you could cast that creature spell. You still pay the spell's costs.)", 'Trample\\nWhenever Primeval Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may search your library for up to two land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Until end of turn, target creature loses all abilities and becomes a blue Frog with base power and toughness 1/1.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Sun Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "When Aether Adept enters the battlefield, return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'When Auramancer enters the battlefield, you may return target enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Goblin Arsonist dies, you may have it deal 1 damage to any target.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Manic Vandal enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact.', 'When Master Thief enters the battlefield, gain control of target artifact for as long as you control Master Thief.', "When Oblivion Ring enters the battlefield, exile another target nonland permanent.\\nWhen Oblivion Ring leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Phantasmal Bear becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Stonehorn Dignitary enters the battlefield, target opponent skips their next combat phase.', 'Whenever Benalish Veteran attacks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever Frost Titan becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter that spell or ability unless its controller pays {2}.\\nWhenever Frost Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, tap target permanent. It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "Whenever a creature an opponent controls becomes tapped, put a +1/+1 counter on Gideon's Avenger.", "Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under an opponent's control, you may have that player lose 1 life.", 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, it deals damage equal to its power to any target.', 'Whenever a creature without flying attacks you or a planeswalker you control, Circle of Flame deals 1 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player taps a land for mana, Manabarbs deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, destroy all permanents other than Worldslayer.\\nEquip {5} ({5}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever you draw a card, you may have target player mill a card.', 'White creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'White creatures you control get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'You gain 1 life for each land you control.', 'You gain 7 life.', 'You may choose new targets for target spell.', 'You may have Phantasmal Image enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it\'s an Illusion in addition to its other types and it has "When this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it."', '[+1]: Chandra, the Firebrand deals 1 damage to any target.\\n[−2]: When you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\n[−6]: Chandra, the Firebrand deals 6 damage to each of up to six targets.', '[+1]: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\n[−3]: Draw cards equal to the greatest power among creatures you control.\\n[−6]: Create a 6/6 green Wurm creature token for each land you control.', '[+1]: Draw a card. Target player mills a card.\\n[0]: Target player mills ten cards.\\n[−7]: Any number of target players each draw twenty cards.', "[+2]: During target opponent's next turn, creatures that player controls attack Gideon Jura if able.\\n[−2]: Destroy target tapped creature.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Gideon Jura becomes a 6/6 Human Soldier creature that's still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.", "[+2]: Sorin Markov deals 2 damage to any target and you gain 2 life.\\n[−3]: Target opponent's life total becomes 10.\\n[−7]: You control target player during that player's next turn.", '{1}, {T}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token. Create five of those tokens instead if you control artifacts named Crown of Empires and Scepter of Empires.', '{1}, {T}: End the turn. Activate only during your turn. (Exile all spells and abilities from the stack. Discard down to your maximum hand size. Damage wears off, and "this turn" and "until end of turn" effects end.)', '{1}{B}: Return Reassembling Skeleton from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', '{1}{B}: Target creature you control gains deathtouch until end of turn. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', '{1}{W}: Target creature you control gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', "{2}, {T}: Reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token. If it's a land card, put that card onto the battlefield under your control. If it's a noncreature, nonland card, you gain 2 life.", "{2}, {T}: You gain 5 life. Shuffle Elixir of Immortality and your graveyard into their owner's library.", '{2}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', "{2}{W}, {T}: Arbalest Elite deals 3 damage to target attacking or blocking creature. Arbalest Elite doesn't untap during your next untap step.", '{3}, {T}: Tap target creature. Gain control of that creature instead if you control artifacts named Scepter of Empires and Throne of Empires.', '{3}{U}: Draw a card.', '{4}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', '{G}: Choose one. Activate only once each turn.\\n• Until end of turn, Skinshifter becomes a Rhino with base power and toughness 4/4 and gains trample.\\n• Until end of turn, Skinshifter becomes a Bird with base power and toughness 2/2 and gains flying.\\n• Until end of turn, Skinshifter becomes a Plant with base power and toughness 0/8.', "{G}: Regenerate Cudgel Troll. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{R}, {T}, Exile two cards from your graveyard: Grim Lavamancer deals 2 damage to any target.', '{R}: Fiery Hellhound gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}: Inferno Titan gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nWhenever Inferno Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, it deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.', '{R}: Target creature you control gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Buried Ruin: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Destroy target tapped creature.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, Goblin Bangchuckers deals 2 damage to any target. If you lose the flip, Goblin Bangchuckers deals 2 damage to itself.', '{T}: Goblin Fireslinger deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', '{T}: Scepter of Empires deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker. It deals 3 damage instead if you control artifacts named Crown of Empires and Throne of Empires.', '{T}: Target creature an opponent controls attacks you this turn if able.', "{T}: Target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{U}, {T}: Each player discards their hand, then draws cards equal to the greatest number of cards a player discarded this way.', '{U}, {T}: Target player mills two cards.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.']
flavor: ['"A world without evil? Boring. Give me vile fiends to smite and banish any day."\\n—Sarlena, paladin of the Northern Verge', '"All your steel won\'t protect you if your will is weak."', '"Any hotheaded cub can raise a sword in anger."', '"Any oaf can conquer a kingdom. It takes true power to conquer time."\\n—Shai Fusan, archmage', '"Bottled life. Not as tasty as I\'m used to, rather stale, but it has the same effect."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Careful. A drop of blood here means death for us all."\\n—Kalek, mountain guide', '"Cherish these last moments. Though your miserable life has come to nothing, I have given it a magnificent end."', '"Dance, and bring forth the coil! It is an umbilical to Gaea herself, fattening us with the earth\'s rich bounty."', '"Don\'t blame me. You\'re the one walking around with skin."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Don\'t you think if I saw a half-woman, half-fish with three glowing eyes, I\'d have remembered?"\\n—Drugo, town guard', '"Every primitive mind has a motive. Easy to find, and eminently exploitable."\\n—Noyan Dar, Tazeem lullmage', '"Fools dig for water, corpses, or gold. The earth\'s real treasure is far deeper."', '"Griffins do not serve. They give freely to those they trust."\\n—Amira, skycaptain of Thune', '"How blessed are some people, whose lives have no fears, no dreads, to whom sleep is a blessing that comes nightly, and brings nothing but sweet dreams."\\n—Bram Stoker, *Dracula*', '"I don\'t know why people say a double-edged sword is bad. It\'s a sword. With two edges."\\n—Kamahl, pit fighter', '"I raised my bow, and the wolf stared at me. Under its gaze, my finger would not release the string."\\n—Aref the Hunter', '"If that is what you seek, try looking in craters."\\n—Fodrus, mastersmith', '"If there is a fire that never ceases to burn, it surely lies in the maw of a dragon."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"In memories, we can find our deepest reserves of strength."', '"Is cold merely the absence of heat, or a force unto itself? Would a display of its power help you decide?"\\n—Zubarek, Icewinder Magus', '"It was too fast, even for our veteran archers. They might as well have been blowing it kisses."\\n—Vulok, elvish archer', '"It\'s actually quite simple, but since you\'ve only recently begun to walk upright, it may take some time to explain."\\n—Jace Beleren, to Garruk Wildspeaker', '"It\'s nothing personal. I\'d just prefer if you weren\'t."\\n—Ashurel, voidmage', '"It\'s time for the \'Smash, Smash\' song!"', '"Let nothing own the skies but the wind."\\n—Dejara, Giltwood druid', '"Let the final vision of doom be etched upon their unblinking eyes."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Listen to the roar! Feel the thunder! The Immersturm shouts its approval with every bolt of lightning!"', '"Of course I\'m sure I\'ve gone mad. The little man who crawled out of my eye was quite clear on this."', '"Oh, it\'s easy enough to kill, but I\'m not going anywhere near it."\\n—Norin the Wary', '"Once he\'s got you, hold on. Fall from a drake and you\'ll suffer much worse than a bruise."\\n—Garl, drake trainer', '"One day I will rest and join my comrades in the afterlife, but not while scum like you still sully this world."', '"Rage courses in every heart, yearning to betray its rational prison."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Removing the encumbrance of useless brain tissue grants several advantages: a slight increase in mobility, a response of revulsion and horror from the enemy, and, in the case of large specimens, room for passengers."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Ribbit."', '"Scholars seek to understand the way the world is. I wish to shape the world into what it should be."', '"Seeing you cower before me is its own reward."', '"Spontaneous combustion is a myth. If you burst into flame, someone wanted you to."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Stop complaining. You can rest when you\'re dead. Oh—sorry."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Tell the cooks to prepare the fires. Tonight we feast!"\\n—Tolar Wolfbrother, Krosan tracker', '"The amphin have long built their society in secret. While surface dwellers squabbled over trivial borders, they patiently expanded, building their ammonite temple-caves. Now amphin priests eye the shore, and amphin hunters gird for war."\\n—Gor Muldrak, *Cryptohistories*', '"The beauty of it is they never see it coming. Ever."\\n—Razzix, sparkmage', '"The best way over the mountain is through."', '"The dream does not end until I say so."', '"The essence of a lawful society is swift deterrence."', '"The forest is my cover and I hold it close. In such a tight embrace, there is no room for wickedness."', '"The gods used their feathers to paint all the colors of the world."\\n—Yare-Tiva, warden of Gramur forest', '"The good don\'t sit and wait for the evil to act. They prepare to defend. They prepare to punish."', '"The key to unlocking this puzzle is within you."\\n—Doriel, mentor of Mistral Isle', '"The past is the foundation for all that exists in the present. We merely reconstruct what our ancestors have already discovered."\\n—Sachimir, Sage of Memories', '"The predator knows the true way of the world. Life is conflict. Only the strong survive."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"The secret to our war paint is hot peppers and stinkbugs. Lots of stinkbugs."\\n—Skab, goblin secretkeeper', '"The southern fortress taken by invaders? Heh, sure . . . when elephants fly."\\n—Brezard Skeinbow, captain of the guard', '"The universe is my instrument, and the song I play upon it is one you are forbidden to hear."', '"The walls of the wicked will fall before us. Ready the siege engines. We proceed to war!"\\n—General Avitora', '"The wild is always changing, but it does have a few constants."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"There is a place deep within my soul where no foe can intrude and no tyrant can conquer."\\n—Sarlena, paladin of the Northern Verge', '"They may show up with the wrong thigh bone or mandible, but they always show up."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"This is a sacred duty. Master Beleren\'s trust has bought an eternity of my loyalty."', '"Those who claim to know the world in its entirety rarely have the requisite perspective."\\n—Ulmarus the Wise', '"To my sword I owe my glory, but to my shield I owe my life."\\n—Sarlena, paladin of the Northern Verge', '"We are one with the wild things. Life blooms from our fingertips and nature responds to our summons."\\n—Jade creed', '"We draw our power from the infinite ocean of the mind, where all manner of things can be conceived."\\n—Azure creed', '"We hold sacred the powers of light and life. Truth and honor are our greatest weapons."\\n—Alabaster creed', '"We wield death and darkness, powers that make lesser mages tremble in fear."\\n—Onyx creed', '"We wield the fires of rage. War is our blood and destruction our birthright."\\n—Crimson creed', '"What do vermin cling to when all hope is lost?"\\n—Sorin Markov', '"When we fail to see the beauty in every tree, we are no better than humans."\\n—Saelia, elvish scout', '"When we of the Northern Verge claim a mount, no peasant\'s nag will do. It must be as strong as our virtue, and must join us of its own will."\\n—Sarlena, paladin of the Northern Verge', '"When you find yourself teetering on the edge of oblivion, mine will be the hands taking pleasure in giving you the final push."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"When your cities and trinkets crumble, only nature will remain."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"Which do you think is a better deterrent: a moat of water or one of fire?"\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Why fight over scraps of land when there\'s so much sky waiting to be claimed?"', '"With this crown, assert your authority."\\n—Crown inscription', '"With this scepter, smite your enemies."\\n—Scepter inscription', '"With this throne, unite your nation."\\n—Throne inscription', '"You clerics brag about your strength of spirit, yet I take away the tiniest fragment, and you crumple like a rag doll."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"You know it to be false, but when its claws find you, what you know won\'t matter much at all."\\n—Pol Jamaar, illusionist', '"You should try to clear your mind of idle thoughts. And if you can\'t, I will."', '"You will kneel before me, even if I have to split the earth under your feet!"\\n—Ash Kronor, Keldon warlord', '"Your superstitions and mumblings are useless chaff before my righteousness."', 'A blazing sun that never sets.', 'A dozen fighting for each other are worth a thousand fighting for themselves.', 'A drop now is all he needs to find you later.', "A griffin is not just an eagle's wings and a lion's claws. It is also the fiercest of hearts.", 'A rock between your eyes hurts. A burning rock between your eyes ruins your whole day.', 'A thin shell lies between the roc and a world of bite-sized treats.', 'About halfway to the target, Snukk vowed that he had been tricked for the last time.', 'After fighting alongside the griffin riders, older knights of Thune learned to admire a mount that could rip an enemy to shreds in seconds.', 'All the trees of the forest are his army, and every leaf his shield.', "An assassin is a king's most trusted courier, ensuring his messages are heard by even the most unwilling recipients.", "Angels appear before both the blessed and the cursed, though most don't know which they are until they feel either the angel's kiss or her sword.", 'Behind every mage is a trail of shattered lies.', 'Blood is holy to those whose god is War.', 'Bone, stone . . . both taste the same to a hungry basilisk.', 'Chandra never believed in using her "inside voice."', 'Death in form and function.', "Don't underestimate the aerodynamic qualities of the common goblin.", 'Empires rise and fall, but evil is eternal.', 'Every grave cradles a recruit.', 'Follow the light. In its absence, follow her.', 'For every action, there is a swifter and more violent reaction.', 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'Ghouls are often found skulking on the fringes of great battles, showing themselves only to snatch the wounded and weak, dragging their victims screaming into the shadows.', 'He knows the name of every elf born in the last four centuries. More importantly, they all know his.', 'He marks his territory with fire and wrath, etching the mountainside with his charring breath.', 'His grim ritual ushers the dead to their new life.', 'History has buried its treasures deep.', "If you have to be stuck somewhere for a while, it's better to be stuck there with a friend.", 'In dark times, Truth bears a blade.', "It can chop down a redwood in a single stroke. Your sternum isn't going to fare any better.", "It did not escape the ambassador's notice that the sound of war drums could also marshal the city to attention.", 'It has to deliberate a moment on the best way to break your face.', 'It makes the insignificant conspicuous, the repulsive alluring, and the deadly irresistible.', 'It stalks the fens by the light of the full moon, gathering shadows as it floats among them.', "It's fun. He doesn't need another reason.", "It's hard enough to find your way through uncharted wilderness when you can see the tip of your nose.", "It's rather embarrassing to end up with your head mounted over his hearth.", "It's seen the wonders of entire worlds trapped in the depths of a bottomless ocean.", "It's so light and fragile that it can glide where the air is thinnest.", 'Its curve mimics the twists of life and death.', 'Its hooves touch the earth only when a hero must rise.', 'Its hunger and ire are no less for being wrought of lies and mist.', "Jevna Nor lugged it around, bragging of his triumph over the wurm. Luckily, the tavern regulars didn't notice it was only a baby tooth.", 'Like most giant monsters villagers worship as gods, it proves a fickle master.', 'Masters of the arcane savor a delicious irony. Their study of deep and complex arcana leads to such a simple end: the ability to say merely yes or no.', 'Merfolk are best known for their subtle magic. But those who try to fight them in their own territory quickly realize that merfolk are hardly defenseless on the field of battle.', "Merfolk don't always know what they're looking for, but they're certain once they find it.", 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', 'Not every thought is a good one.', 'Once a griffin sentinel adopts a territory as its own, only death can force it to betray its post.', "Once he'd worked out which end of the thing was sharp, he was promoted to guard duty.", 'One bone broken for every twig snapped underfoot.\\n—Llanowar penalty for trespassing', "One thing's for sure—his fists are harder than your skull.", 'Planeswalkers seek out great monuments throughout the Multiverse, knowing that their builders were unknowingly drawn by the convergence of mana in the area.', 'Possession is ten-tenths of the law.', 'She lures victims with promises of flesh, captures them in a net of deceit, and destroys them in the embrace of the sea.', 'Sins that would be too gruesome in the light of day are made more pleasing in the dark of night.', 'Some of the eleven minotaur clans of Mirtiin are expert crafters and learned philosophers. Others just like to hit stuff.', 'Sometimes a little chaos is in order.', 'Sometimes an eruption in Shiv produces something more dangerous than a mere river of molten rock.', 'Such loyalty can only be made.', 'Take away a few things, and a rebellion may ensue. Take away everything, and the oppression will be accepted as fate.', 'The angel represents divine perfection; even the smallest feather is imbued with beauty and benevolence.', 'The creations of the hand are confined by reality. The creations of the mind know no such limits.', 'The fatal flaw in every plan is the assumption that you know more than your enemy.', 'The foolish try to leap through the unlit spaces. The arrogant believe the fires harmless. The wise find a different door.', 'The gods are not always kind, but they do have a soft spot for plucky underdogs.', 'The golems of the ancient Thran still draw power in ways that baffle the artificers of today.', "The gorger's insect-like eyes pick up the slightest movement in any direction. Its body then whips toward its prey with startling speed, swallowing it in one engulfing gulp.", 'The juiciest prey is that which grows lazy, thinking itself beyond the reach of danger.', 'The litany of the infernal on his flesh pulses to the beating of his dark heart.', 'The mage breathed in life-giving air and breathed out death-bringing fire.', 'The most genteel facades hide the most abominable desires.', "The nomads' funeral pyres are more practical than ceremonial.", 'The only blow that matters is the killing blow.', 'The only honey it wants is the sweet nectar flowing through your veins.', 'The pup looked over the treetops, eyeing the man who just yesterday had kicked her. Suddenly, her hunger was infused with pure delight.', 'The quickest way to get through the jungle is to agitate a rhino and run in its wake.', "The rustling of leaves and a passing shadow are a dryad's only trace.", 'The shield of unimpeachable purity is as strong as any wrought on the anvil.', 'The spoils of war are not measured only in gold and silver.', 'The swamps go silent at its approach, but it still hears the heartbeat of the prey within.', 'The vanguard is skilled at waging war alone. The enemy is often defeated before its reinforcements reach the front.', 'The wise always keep an ear open to the whispers of power.', 'The wise pay as much attention to what they throw away as to what they keep.', 'Their arrival is heralded by the deafening hum of ten thousand wings. Their departure is marked by the silence of the dead.', 'There are few things as satisfying as a good, healthy thunk.', "There's nothing more exciting than a game of fetch the still-beating heart.", 'Those who examine the amulet too closely have been known to become part of its ornate carvings.', 'Those who raged most bitterly at the world in life are cursed to roam the nether realms in death.', 'Together the soldiers were like a golden blade, cutting down their enemies and scarring the darkness.', 'Tomorrow belongs to those who prepare for it today.', "What's scarier than one of every beast in the forest?", 'When he began to curse what he held holy, his strength grew unrivaled.', 'When nature calls, *run*.', 'With an armory of light, even the squire may champion her people.', 'With great power comes great risk of getting yourself killed.']
artist: ['Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Allen Williams', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Ash Wood', 'Austin Hsu', 'Brad Rigney', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Charles Urbach', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'D. J. Cleland-Hura', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Dorman', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'E. M. Gist', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Ryman', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'Jon Foster', 'Jung Park', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kekai Kotaki', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Marcelo Vignali', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Nic Klein', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paolo Parente', 'Paul Bonner', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Rob Alexander', 'Robert Bliss', 'Robh Ruppel', 'Ron Spears', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Wood', 'Steve Luke', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Ted Galaday', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Véronique Meignaud', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'jD', 'rk post']
